966,0,0,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,58,null,null],[138649908,"Blue and red nails",null,0,0,null,14,null,null,null,0,0,55,null,"GMTT 1221"],[142280914,"La Proue de la Table",1967,0,0,null,15,null,null,null,0,0,null,null,null]],"summaryBase":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/","summaryLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","summaries":{"2974254":["Cirque Calder is an artistic rendering and performance of a circus created by the American artist Alexander Calder through the late 1920s. It involves wire models rigged to perform the various functions of the circus performers they represent, from contortionists to sword eaters to lion tamers.","Cirque Calder"],"3073296":["Flamingo, a sculpture by American artist Alexander Calder, is a 53-foot-tall (16 m) stabile located in the Federal Plaza in front of the Kluczynski Federal Building in Chicago, Illinois, United States.","Flamingo (sculpture)"],"3983835":["Teodelapio is the only monumental stabile sculpture in Italy by Alexander Calder. Situated in Spoleto it was designed and donated to the city for the 1962 edition of Festival dei Due Mondi.","Teodelapio"],"5094279":["Cheval Rouge is an abstract sculpture by Alexander Calder.","Cheval Rouge"],"5324996":["Eagle is an abstract sculpture by Alexander Calder. It is located at the Olympic Sculpture Park, Seattle.","Eagle (Calder)"],"5463397":["Flying Dragon is a sculpture by Alexander Calder in the Art Institute of Chicago North Stanley McCormick Memorial Court north of the Art Institute of Chicago Building in the Loop community area of Chicago, Illinois.","Flying Dragon (Calder)"],"5623517":["Gwenfritz is a painted steel abstract stabile, by Alexander Calder. It is located at the National Museum of American History, at 14th Street, and Constitution Avenue, in Washington, D.C.","Gwenfritz"],"5711801":["The Aula Magna is an auditorium at the Central University of Venezuela. It is located within the University City of Caracas, next to the University's main library building.","Aula Magna (Central University of Venezuela)"],"6462864":["La Grande Vitesse, a public sculpture by American artist Alexander Calder, is located on the large concrete plaza surrounding City Hall and the Kent County Building in Grand Rapids, Michigan, United States.","La Grande Vitesse"],"6663853":["Lobster Trap and Fish Tail, a mobile by American artist Alexander Calder, is located at the Museum of Modern Art in New York City, New York, United States.","Lobster Trap and Fish Tail"],"6828745":["Homage to Jerusalem is a 1977 sculpture by Alexander Calder in Holland Square, near Mount Herzl in Jerusalem. It is at the corner of Kiryat Yovel Street and Ein Karem at a view point overlooking the Jerusalem Forest.","Homage to Jerusalem"],"6925686":["Mountains and Clouds is a sculpture by Alexander Calder located in the Hart Senate Office Building.","Mountains and Clouds"],"7537350":["Sky Hooks is a painted sheet steel sculpture by Alexander Calder, constructed in 1962. It is located at the Hirshhorn Museum and Sculpture Garden.","Sky Hooks"],"10467354":["The Four Elements is a monumental mobile sculpture created by the American sculptor Alexander Calder in 1961. The sculpture is a motorized moving group of four metal sheets.","The Four Elements (sculpture)"],"16951232":["Bent Propeller was a red stainless steel sculpture by Alexander Calder.","Bent Propeller"],"21188883":["The Crab is an outdoor 1962 painted steel sculpture by Alexander Calder, installed outside the Museum of Fine Arts, Houston, in the U.S. state of Texas. It measures 120 inches (3.0 m) x 240 inches (6.1 m) x 120 inches (3.0 m) inches.","The Crab (sculpture)"],"55123016":["The Whirling Ear is a 1958 sculpture by Alexander Calder, installed in Brussels. It was made using sheet metal and paint, with motor.","The Whirling Ear"],"74254554":["Floating Clouds is a work of art by American sculptor Alexander Calder, located in the Aula Magna of the University City of Caracas in Venezuela. The 1953 work comprises many 'cloud' panels that are renowned both artistically and acoustically.","Floating Clouds (artwork)"],"85775400":["La Grande Voile (The Big Sail), sometimes translated The Great Sail, is a 1965 painted steel sculpture by Alexander Calder, installed in McDermott Court on the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) campus in Cambridge, Massachusetts, United States.","La Grande Voile (The Big Sail)"],"93632932":["The Snow Flurry design was used by American artist Alexander Calder for at least seven mobiles between 1948 and 1959. A monumental design composed of white disks of varying sizes are connected on different branches and levels to reflect a snow flurry in Calder's distinct Modernist style.","Snow Flurry (design)"],"107736059":["El Sol Rojo is an outdoor steel sculpture in Mexico City. It was created by the American artist Alexander Calder for the 1968 Summer Olympics, specifically for the Ruta de la Amistad art project, and it was installed on the grounds of Estadio Azteca.","El Sol Rojo"]},"titlesFrom":["fr","P1476","alias:en","alias:fr","aliasFilter:1"]}